    {
        "sha": "d2f2439ecf5d5c70dbc25f635729a9ea17fe61a3",
        "node_id": "C_kwDOQ8XTDdoAKGQyZjI0MzllY2Y1ZDVjNzBkYmMyNWY2MzU3MjlhOWVhMTdmZTYxYTM",
        "commit": {
            "author": {
                "name": "Linus Torvalds",
                "email": "torvalds@linux-foundation.org",
                "date": "2026-01-18T21:55:16Z"
            },
            "committer": {
                "name": "Linus Torvalds",
                "email": "torvalds@linux-foundation.org",
                "date": "2026-01-18T21:55:16Z"
            },
            "message": "Stop being quite so lazy about line lengths and UTF-8\n\nThis deals with line lengths by ignoring the issue and just using a\nstate machine on raw buffers.\n\nIt also deals with UTF-8 content using exactly the same \"ignore it\" way:\njust blithely assume that any non-US-ASCII characters are just letters\nin other alphabets.\n\nBecause ignorance is bliss, and that makes it do the right thing for\nFinnish and Swedish.  And presumably other languages that I don't speak\ntoo.\n\nOf course, if you use use other encodings than UTF-8, you get what you\ndeserve.  And even with UTF-8, this will get other Unicode things like\nhalf-space characters etc wrong, and just consider it all part of the\nword, and call you out on your odd spelling.\n\nYou win some, you lose some.  I'm not interested in doing an actual full\nUnicode lookup thing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Linus Torvalds <torvalds@linux-foundation.org>",
