    {
        "sha": "bc93b5011e24b56211ec806e0a1697d8ef3278d3",
        "node_id": "C_kwDOQ8XTDdoAKGJjOTNiNTAxMWUyNGI1NjIxMWVjODA2ZTBhMTY5N2Q4ZWYzMjc4ZDM",
        "commit": {
            "author": {
                "name": "Linus Torvalds",
                "email": "torvalds@linux-foundation.org",
                "date": "2026-01-18T19:53:56Z"
            },
            "committer": {
                "name": "Linus Torvalds",
                "email": "torvalds@linux-foundation.org",
                "date": "2026-01-18T19:53:56Z"
            },
            "message": "Do a really simple colorizing pager\n\nThis *must* exist somewhere, but google failed me and couldn't find it.\n\nI want a simple pager that shows me my typos in commit messages etc.  I\nreally should just integrate this into my editor instead, since that's\nthe real problem here (and my fingers refuse to learn new things:\nbelieve me, I've tried), but I decided that the first step would be to\njust do a minimal wrapper around the hunspell library to at least learn\nhow to use it.\n\nThis thing just exec's 'less' to do the actual paging, and inserts\nitself as a pipe between stdin and less. So you can do\n\n\texport LESS=-FRSX\n\texport GIT_PAGER=huncolor\n\nand you are more or less done.\n\nWell, you'd be done if this was slightly better - it doesn't do very\nwell with code etc.  It's not *horrible*, and mostly works together with\nthe native colorization, but it's not great either.  I might improve it,\nbut as a proof-of-concept this is about as simple as it gets.\n\n[ The \"build system\" is also as simple as it gets, and hardcodes the\n  hunspell version etc. I can't find it in myself to care right now ]\n\nSigned-off-by: Linus Torvalds <torvalds@linux-foundation.org>",
            "tree": {
                "sha": "f83358a404f4d48f6307dba2c14e7fa755028a7f",
                "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/torvalds/HunspellColorize/git/trees/f83358a404f4d48f6307dba2c14e7fa755028a7f"
